## 2. Google Sheet Column Layout & Field Mapping

Column **A** (`Mess ID`) serves as the unique primary key. Any sync operation looks up Column A to determine whether to update an existing row or append a new one.

| Column | Field Name | Firestore Field (Mess / Room) | Editable in Sheet? | Sample Value |
| :---: | :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |
| **A** | `Mess ID` | `mess.id` | ❌ **No (Anchor Key)** | `mess_x9y2z1` |
| **B** | `Mess Name` | `mess.name` | ✍️ Yes | `Maa Tarini Mess` |
| **C** | `Contact Number` | `mess.contact` | ✍️ Yes | `9876543210` |
| **D** | `District` | `mess.district` | ✍️ Yes | `balasore` |
| **E** | `City` | `mess.city` | ✍️ Yes | `remuna` |
| **F** | `Locality` | `mess.locality` | ✍️ Yes | `Station Road` |
| **G** | `Address` | `mess.address` | ✍️ Yes | `Near Railway Gate, Plot 14` |
| **H** | `Gender / Type` | `mess.messType` | ✍️ Yes | `Boys` |
| **I** | `Food Facility` | `mess.foodAvailability` / `foodFacility` | ✍️ Yes | `3 Meals (Veg + Non-Veg)` |
| **J** | `Security Deposit` | `mess.securityDeposit` | ✍️ Yes | `1 Month` |
| **K** | `Rent Cycle` | `mess.rentCycle` | ✍️ Yes | `monthly` |
| **L** | `Single Bed Rent` | `room (Single).price` | ✍️ Yes | `3500` |
| **M** | `Double Bed Rent` | `room (Double).price` | ✍️ Yes | `2200` |
| **N** | `Triple Bed Rent` | `room (Triple).price` | ✍️ Yes | `1800` |
| **O** | `Total Vacancies` | Sum of `room.availableCount` | ✍️ Yes | `4` |
| **P** | `Status` | `mess.hidden` (`false`=Live, `true`=Hidden) | ✍️ Yes | `Live` |
| **Q** | `Google Maps URL` | `mess.locationUrl` / Computed coordinates | ✍️ Yes | `https://maps.google.com/?q=...` |
| **R** | `Last Synced At` | Timestamp string | ❌ System | `2026-10-07 11:30 AM` |
| **S+** | *Operator Remarks* | *None (Sheet Only)* | ✍️ Yes | *“Called on Oct 5. Owner confirmed seats.”* |

> **Note on Custom Columns (S+)**: The Google Apps Script only writes to Columns A through R. Any custom columns you add on the right (notes, caller history, payment tracking) **will remain untouched and intact** across all sync operations.

