## 6. Edge Cases & Safeguards

| Potential Scenario | How It Is Guarded |
| :--- | :--- |
| **New Mess C Registered 2 days later** | The script matches Column A (`Mess ID`). Mess A and B are updated in place; Mess C does not exist in the index map and is appended at the bottom. |
| **Repeated Sync Clicks** | Clicking sync multiple times has zero duplicate effect because existing IDs match and simply overwrite the row values. |
| **Custom Operator Notes (Columns S, T, etc.)** | The update range in Apps Script is constrained to `1` through `rowValues.length`. Any notes written in subsequent columns are preserved. |
| **Concurrent Operator Edits** | Google Apps Script uses `LockService.getScriptLock()` to queue requests and prevent write collisions. |
| **Accidental Sheet Typos** | The Diff Review Modal shows old vs. new values before anything is written to Firestore. |

